WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:05.933
HIPAA training. Module 5. Business associates and the agreements behind your work.

2
00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:14.000
A business associate does work for a covered entity that involves patient information.

3
00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:16.733
ERS is one for many of its clients.

4
00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:22.733
The clinic shares information only after a signed agreement.

5
00:00:23.067 --> 00:00:28.733
ERS needs an agreement with each vendor it uses.

6
00:00:29.067 --> 00:00:31.800
The same restrictions follow down the chain.

7
00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:36.600
Use information only as the contract allows.

8
00:00:36.933 --> 00:00:39.033
Use appropriate safeguards.

9
00:00:39.367 --> 00:00:43.967
Report any use the contract does not allow, including breaches.

10
00:00:44.333 --> 00:00:47.833
Make subcontractors agree to the same restrictions.

11
00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:54.867
A business associate reports a breach without unreasonable delay, and within 60 days at most.

12
00:00:55.233 --> 00:00:59.600
So report a possible incident internally the same day.

13
00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:01.367
Stop.

14
00:01:01.767 --> 00:01:02.767
Do not share.

15
00:01:03.167 --> 00:01:04.300
Ask your lead.

16
00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:06.433
Now read the module.
